crates/parametric-eq/tests/silent_fixed_point.rs-16-//! holds — forces the slow path on every block without moving a bit. That the redundant point is
crates/parametric-eq/tests/silent_fixed_point.rs-17-//! itself bit-neutral is not assumed here: it is exactly what `stationary_hoist.rs` proves, and
crates/parametric-eq/tests/silent_fixed_point.rs-18-//! that test is the one that fails if the assumption ever stops holding.
crates/parametric-eq/tests/silent_fixed_point.rs-19-//!
crates/parametric-eq/tests/silent_fixed_point.rs-20-//! The signal is deliberately tone-then-silence-then-tone. The leading tone drives the
crates/parametric-eq/tests/silent_fixed_point.rs-21-//! integrators somewhere nonzero, the silence is long enough for them to settle and for the claim
crates/parametric-eq/tests/silent_fixed_point.rs-22-//! to be earned, and the trailing tone is what catches a fast path that corrupted or froze the
crates/parametric-eq/tests/silent_fixed_point.rs-23-//! state it skipped over: if the skipped blocks left the filter in the wrong place, the tone that
crates/parametric-eq/tests/silent_fixed_point.rs-24-//! follows them renders differently.
